cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TEF Emulator to produce research results, please cite the
  software version used.
  When a Zenodo archive is available, cite the version-specific DOI for
  the release you used. Cite the relevant TEF papers separately for
  their theoretical contributions.
type: software
title: "TEF Emulator"
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Xiaodan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5892-0293"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-emergent-frame/tef-emulator"
url: "https://github.com/the-emergent-frame/tef-emulator"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TEF Emulator is an experimental, event-driven computational laboratory
  for exploring candidate spacetime rollout rules in The Emergent Frame.
  A Rust reference engine records local state transitions and causal
  dependencies, Python supports reproducible experiments and verification,
  and a browser observer provides interactive replay and diagnostics.
  The initial experiment models a persistent source extending independent
  channels, with an explicitly assumed isotropic three-dimensional observer
  representation. Matter formation and physical energy transfer remain
  open modeling questions. The current scaffold and engineering controls
  do not establish an independent physical finding.
keywords:
  - The Emergent Frame
  - spacetime rollout
  - event-driven simulation
  - causal histories
  - computational physics
  - reproducible research

